course: dictionary
lesson: 6850
title: Outsmart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To outsmart someone is to beat them by being cleverer or trickier. You do not need to be bigger or stronger to outsmart someone. You need a better plan.
explain: Look at «Unlike Jerry, a real mouse cannot outsmart a cat with an iron». The word tells you the mouse wins by thinking, not by fighting. Ask yourself: who has the better plan here?
explain: Outsmart is a verb, so it changes: outsmart, outsmarts, outsmarted, outsmarting. The phrase «be outsmarted by» means someone else had the better plan and won.
fact: To outsmart means to beat someone by being cleverer or trickier.
fact: Outsmart is a verb: outsmart, outsmarts, outsmarted, outsmarting.
fact: «Outsmart the fox» means trick a sly animal with a better plan.
fact: Small, clever characters often outsmart bigger ones in stories, like the Gruffalo's mouse and Brer Rabbit.
fact: Scammers try to outsmart people, so learning their tricks helps keep you safe.
exercise: «Unlike Jerry, a real mouse cannot outsmart a cat with an iron.» What does outsmart mean here? | To hug someone warmly | To make someone laugh | To run faster than someone in a race | *To beat someone by being cleverer or trickier
exercise: Kai says the mouse won because it was bigger. What is wrong with his idea? | Outsmart means sleeping through a fight | Outsmart means being very slow | Outsmart means being bigger than your opponent | *Outsmart means winning by being cleverer, not bigger
exercise: Find the phrase from the sentences that means someone else had the better plan. | teeth that never stop growing | *be outsmarted by | songs too high for us to hear | secret food stores
test: Yesterday the fox ___ the hounds by hiding in the stream. | outsmart | *outsmarted | outsmarts | outsmarting
test: Every day the clever mouse ___ the sleepy cat with a new plan. | outsmarting | *outsmarts | outsmarted | outsmart
exam: Which of these is a safety lesson about people trying to outsmart you? | A recipe for pancakes | A song about the sea | A library book about birds | *A scammer who tries to trick you with a fake prize
